# GameTrack Web

This repository contains the React frontend for GameTrack. Its sibling API is
maintained independently at:
https://github.com/LucasCruz2773/game-tracker-api

Use Node.js 24. Do not downgrade it or change the configured engine/version
unless explicitly requested.

## Architecture

- React, TypeScript, Vite, React Router and Tailwind CSS
- Organize code by feature: auth, games, library, reviews and dashboard
- Use TanStack Query for server state
- Use local state for local UI; add Zustand only for genuine shared client state
- The frontend communicates exclusively through the backend REST API
- Never import backend/database models or expose external API credentials
- Handle loading, error and empty states and keep the UI responsive

The backend OpenAPI document is the source of truth for the HTTP contract.
When a full-stack change is needed, use a corresponding branch and cross-link
the pull requests in both repositories.

## Development

- Build incrementally and avoid premature abstractions
- Preserve strict typing and avoid `any`
- Add meaningful component/unit/E2E tests for important user flows
- Do not rewrite unrelated code
- Keep `.env` untracked and document configuration in `.env.example`
- Before adding a dependency, confirm current stable support for Node.js 24

Use small Conventional Commits, for example `feat(library): add status filter`.
Run Git commands in this repository, not in the parent workspace.

Current priority: keep the existing MVP production-ready before adding social,
queue, recommendation or AI features.
